{
  "version": 3,
  "title": "Why You Don't Want X-Ray Vision",
  "series": "Low Poly Shorts",
  "style": "lowpoly_shorts",
  "pacing": "viral_shorts",
  "narratorStyle": "urgent",
  "speechRate": 1.48,
  "narration": "If you had x-ray vision, you'd think you could see through walls and stuff, but you'd actually be better off without it for many reasons. The moment it happens, you'd just see black. See, your boring old eyes only work cause light bounces off objects and into them. But nothing around you gives off x-rays, so there'd be nothing to see. But what if instead of looking at the x-rays around you, you could shoot the x-rays from your eyes and detect them? Well, unlike a normal light that bounces around, most x-rays would go right through the object you're trying to see without bouncing back, so you'd only see black again. Not to mention that if you looked at someone long enough, you'd give them cancer. But there's a solution for this too: you'll just need to get a friend that can stand on the other side of whatever you're trying to look at, pointing an x-ray detector at your face all day, every day. But then your friend's the one who'd get to see, not you.",
